{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2023-12-11","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2031-09-30","@type":"3"}],"/activity-status@code":"2","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"WCA","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"b.assande@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Assande, Brou Arsene","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The development objective of LYSP is to improve the livelihoods of the target groups, promote their economic and climatic resilience and improve their food and nutritional security.\n\nThe project is expected to produce the following impacts: (i) 80 per cent of supported households will report an increase in income; (ii) the nutritional status \nand climate resilience of supported households will have been improved; and (iii) 2,802 stable jobs will have been created, including 1,121 for young people.The project will insure provision of adequate rural infrastructures  for the development of  livestock and fish sub sectors  alone the value chain from production to market and processing. This include services for pest and disease  management. \n\nThe project is intended to livestock producers, crop producers, fishermen, bees keepers  living in targeted rural areas. Related farmers organisations will constitute keys elements of the project stakeholders in order to support the sustainability of investments and ownership of producers.The project will promote a sustainable natural resources management  by supporting pastoral systems and  insuring an integrated health and  husbandry practices as well as community awareness on communal pastoral resources. This involves others resources users such as crop producers and fishermen.   \nThe project will insure  development of a sustainable use of pastoral resources and development of breeding system adapted to the environment  It will also promote and support  water, fodder and land usage association for sustainable natural resource management. It will also have better consideration of the use of animal organic manure in the soil fertility management mechanism through capacity building of producers and POs on composting, support local bio-fertilizer production and use through composting and use of biodigesters","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A03"},{"@code":"A04"},{"@code":"A05"},{"@code":"A06"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Central African Republic 2000004022: PEAJ Project Design Report October 2023","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/c468e41c-3fa0-4af2-9c89-bba6e1d2bd18"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Central African Republic 2000004022: LYSP Supervision Report January 2025","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/43d5cb17-9b64-419e-98c3-dcb546bbec5b"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Central African Republic 2000004022: LYSP Supervision Report January 2026","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/95b6c9f1-49b0-4139-955e-1570e8c83034"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of development.","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"IATI documentation on IFAD corporate website","@xml:l